<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Corpgro year net eps 1.31 cents.</title>
<headline>Corpgro year net eps 1.31 cents.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 vs six months to September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		 1.31	 vs   0.64</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   15.76	 vs   5.23</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   23.76	 vs   8.05</p>
<p>    Tax			  8.00	 vs   2.82</p>
<p>    Interest received	1.43	 vs   0.07 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		 233.35	 vs   76.95</p>
<p>Full name: Corpgro Ltd (shares)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company did not provide comparable results for the year to March 1996, but said its operating performance was well ahead of budget.</p>
<p>Chief executive, Jeff Liebesman said he expected substantial real EPS growth.</p>
<p>Corpgro said the group had strong cash balances in anticipation of further acquisitions in the short term.</p>
<p>The company plans a nine-for-one share consolidation resulting in about 200 million shares on issue. It will declare annual dividends at its year end, which will change to August 31 from that date onward.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
